WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A picture can hold exactly the same parts and still look completely different when you turn it around.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1980, Peter Thompson described a face illusion: altered eyes and mouth become much stranger when the whole face is upright.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Later research found related effects in objects and showed the explanation is more complicated than a face-only switch.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
An illusion is evidence about perception, not proof that a sound recording can change your brain.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
If you want a short listening routine, compare the actual package, free alternatives and what science has tested.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the sources and try the free twelve-minute observation before choosing any product.
